# v-env AT ITS PLACE: THE PRODUCT'S RELIGHTING READS WHERE THE GENERATED FRAME STANDS (2026-10-18, frame generation phase 5, the true
# fill's package G1, part 3: docs\reports\fg-5\brief-truefill\BRIEF-G1-lib.md). ON TOP OF v-env, IN ITS TEXT. EXACT AT THE
# MIDDLE: every number it changes is v-env's own there, by a test of the constant or a product by 1.
#
# WHAT v-env DID AT A PLACE OTHER THAN THE MIDDLE (read 2026-10-18; v-env.cut's own head: "not yet position-aware"). Since the cut
# fi-position the game's field stores S = MV * (1 - t), the way from the current frame's place to the generated frame's;
# the interpolation fetches the CURRENT frame's colour at minus S and the PREVIOUS frame's at S * t / (1 - t)
# (PositionToPrevious()). v-env, written for the middle, where both are S:
#   1. relit the PREVIOUS sample for a fetch place of plus S, not where it was fetched: at t = 1/3 S is two thirds of the
#      vector and the sample was fetched a third of it away (the envelopes were read a third of the vector too far), at
#      2/3 S is a third and the sample was fetched two thirds away (read a third too near). The current sample's place was
#      right at every t;
#   2. LEANED TO THE MIDDLE: where it relit a pixel whose two samples it believes alike, the blend became 0.5
#      (fEnvT = trust of the current / both trusts), pulled from the frame's own t by the pixel's share fEnvShare. At 1/3
#      and 2/3 a fully relit pixel stood half way between the two real frames, not at its place;
#   3. measured "a sample that hardly moves" (mend 2) by S, which is the half vector only at the middle (at 1/3 it is two
#      thirds of the vector, at 2/3 a third).
# THE CUT, three places of v-env's text and nothing else:
#   1. the previous sample's envelopes at plus S * PositionToPrevious() (1 by a test at the middle: S * 1 is S);
#   2. the two trusts weighed by where the frame stands, fEnvT = t * trust_current / ((1 - t) * trust_previous +
#      t * trust_current): at equal trust the blend is t, and the sample that needed less relighting is believed more,
#      as before. At the middle v-env's own expression, by a test of the constant;
#   3. mend 2's half vector is half of the whole vector, S * (PositionWhole() * 0.5): PositionWhole() is 2 at the middle by a
#      test, so the factor is exactly 1.
# WHAT IT COSTS: the constant is in the constant buffer the interpolation pass has bound already (fi-position's spare word);
# two tests of it, a multiply of a vector by it, a few more products where a pixel is relit. Measured by the stamps
# (tools\test-fg-own\fgtime.cpp; G1's report of 2026-10-18 has the numbers).
# THE JUDGE: at the middle the product's pictures must be the pinned ones (tools\test-fg-own\run.py --ours, step 9): the pin
# is NOT made again for this cut. At another place it changes the picture (tools\test-fg-own\thirds.py --env says where):
# nobody but the owner judges a picture at a third (the true fill's leg 6, thirds by eye on a fixed screen).
what v-env reads where the generated frame stands: the previous sample's envelopes at its own fetch place, the two samples' trusts weighed by the frame's place, mend 2's half vector the whole vector's half; exactly v-env at the middle
passes ffx_frameinterpolation_pass
wave64 it edits ffx_frameinterpolation.h, which both the cs_6_2 and the cs_6_6 (wave64) variants of the interpolation pass are compiled from; no wave operation; not run here on a wave64 device
file framegeneration/fsr3/include/gpu/frameinterpolation/ffx_frameinterpolation.h
--- old
    const FfxFloat32x2 fHalf  = fHalfUv * fSize;
--- new
    // (the mod's cut v-env-position) the half of the WHOLE vector, at any place of the generated frame (S at the middle: the factor is 1 there)
    const FfxFloat32x2 fHalf  = fHalfUv * (PositionWhole() * 0.5f) * fSize;
--- end
file framegeneration/fsr3/include/gpu/frameinterpolation/ffx_frameinterpolation.h
--- old
    fBelievedPrev.x = envOne(fLogPlace, SampleEnvCurrent((fUv + fHalfUv) * fScale.xy), ENV_GAIN_MOST, fNeedPrev.x);
--- new
    // (the mod's cut v-env-position) the previous sample was fetched at plus S * PositionToPrevious() (1 at the middle by a test)
    const FfxFloat32x2 fPrevFetchUv = fUv + fHalfUv * PositionToPrevious();
    fBelievedPrev.x = envOne(fLogPlace, SampleEnvCurrent(fPrevFetchUv * fScale.xy), ENV_GAIN_MOST, fNeedPrev.x);
--- end
file framegeneration/fsr3/include/gpu/frameinterpolation/ffx_frameinterpolation.h
--- old
    const FfxFloat32x4 fTintPrev  = SampleEnvTintCurrent((fUv + fHalfUv) * fScale.zw);
--- new
    const FfxFloat32x4 fTintPrev  = SampleEnvTintCurrent(fPrevFetchUv * fScale.zw);    // (the mod's cut v-env-position)
--- end
file framegeneration/fsr3/include/gpu/frameinterpolation/ffx_frameinterpolation.h
--- old
    fEnvT = fTrustCurr / (fTrustPrev + fTrustCurr);
--- new
    // (the mod's cut v-env-position) the trusts weighed by where the frame stands: at equal trust the blend is the frame's own t;
    // at the middle v-env's own expression, by a test of the constant
    const FfxFloat32 fPosition = InterpolationPosition();
    fEnvT = (fPosition == 0.5f) ? fTrustCurr / (fTrustPrev + fTrustCurr)
                                : (fPosition * fTrustCurr) / ((1.0f - fPosition) * fTrustPrev + fPosition * fTrustCurr);
--- end
